{"title":"What I’ve been reading","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/925707980/0/marginalrevolution~What-Ive-been-reading.html","date":1759468809000,"content":"<p>Marcus Willaschek, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Kant-Revolution-Thinking-Marcus-Willaschek/dp/0674296109/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2KM22PTJCYK0H&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.LBLvRDUBhi66-X5R94702mcXzmGeIAeUyw7qZC3bEM6k91nNaODGdbT9dwTV5JA_nBx4sDZnfA0EE1L0hB2igU0IWD2e-YjcG4bFaC-f5h7S5Ht0zVIXp2b_pQhGrnf6.e0upJxaxb0VQxlCA1n2GnlN7QGWf1kxKavLMRevOlkI&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Kant%3A+A+Revolution+in+Thinking&amp;qid=1759277986&amp;sprefix=kant+a+revolution+in+thinking%2Caps%2C64&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Kant: A Revolution in Thinking</a>.  A very good book, perhaps the best introduction to Kant?  Though for me it is mostly interior to my current knowledge set.</p>\r\n<p>Matthew Bell, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Goeths-8211-Life-Ideas/dp/0691153957/ref=sr_1_1?crid=372UNMAM11EGS&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.9h9rc1iMq_xjEng4SuAr6L0TqYYor7KUAZFJM7ltAahe14mGyHBOWHFcGxC-cXwwGffe-Iqihg47QZY-5sFWxw.J4YkvDxBaq_0XRx2qnyXtWlDXQOWvoyWP8mY9uQ1GHw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Goethe%3A+A+Life+in+Ideas&amp;qid=1759278052&amp;sprefix=goethe+a+life+in+ideas%2Caps%2C104&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Goethe: A Life in Ideas</a>.  A beautiful book, now in English we have Nicholas Boyle’s work and also this.  Bell is wise enough to understand and value<em> Iphigenia auf Tauris</em>, a good test for Goethe appeciation.  Although I had a library copy out to read, I went ahead and bought a copy of this one to own.</p>\r\n<p>Benjamin Wilson, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Strange-Stability-Scientists-Control-Military-Industrial/dp/0674976088/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2DMSSKMETUA3Z&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.MYmf4H8xZvQI8OtLVIHCNw.IByGmRvI0TSv7BBv-UtBVidKDuQhtSGAaoybaL7vW7A&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Strange+Stability%3A+How+Cold+War+Scientists+Set+Out+to+Control+the+Arms+Race+and+Ended+up+Serving+the+Military-Industrial+Complex&amp;qid=1759278088&amp;sprefix=strange+stability+how+cold+war+scientists+set+out+to+control+the+arms+race+and+ended+up+serving+the+military-industrial+complex%2Caps%2C107&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Stability: How Cold War Scientists Set Out to Control the Arms Race and Ended up Serving the Military-Industrial Complex</a> is both interesting and has plenty of information on early Thomas Schelling and his precursors.</p>\r\n<p>Very well researched is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Highest-Exam-Gaokao-Shapes-China/dp/0674295390/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3SJIITI3TSPS8&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.Vjz6OHdP0kgITvahjC8GJg.pSpwZtSeXo2q8HZ0N2000GmH01A7DoltinzLMUHyxrE&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Highest+Exam%3A+How+the+Gaokao+Shapes+China&amp;qid=1759278125&amp;sprefix=the+highest+exam+how+the+gaokao+shapes+china%2Caps%2C74&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">The Highest Exam: How the Gaokao Shapes China</a>, by Ruixue Jia and Hongbin Li, with Claire Cousineau.</p>\r\n<p>Peter Baxter, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Rhodesia-Complete-1890-1980-Peter-Baxter/dp/1726710629/ref=sr_1_1?crid=YBEOHZDV4S00&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.ggan9dblFKquXOBwfT42fA.F4Aws7j_eGzkLAugWtKzsVz5Cm9E3nPLUW3Kv5pmMGA&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Rhodesia%3A+A+Complete+History+1890-1980&amp;qid=1759277950&amp;sprefix=rhodesia+a+complete+history+1890-1980%2Caps%2C58&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Rhodesia: A Complete History 1890-1980</a>.  The most complete history of the country I have been able to find.  Many of the other books contain a few dominant, non-false narratives, but one gets tired of that?  I say LLMs come especially in handy for learning this history.</p>\r\n<p>Luka Ivan Jukic, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Central-Europe-Death-Civilization-Life/dp/1911723987/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3G55WTXSUR0G8&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.DNoyseekFYJhaWHbWfzy8A.2-MJq-6YLWZGLR0KKXMeiPKqP61BW_j3RlUnmb7H4Ko&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Central+Europe%3A+The+Death+of+a+Civilization+and+the+Life+of+an+Idea&amp;qid=1759277885&amp;sprefix=central+europe+the+death+of+a+civilization+and+the+life+of+an+idea%2Caps%2C89&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Central Europe: The Death of a Civilization and the Life of an Idea</a>.  I took this sentence to encapsulate the main lesson of the book, namely that this does not usually work: “Central Europeans were, as ever, masterfully adept at rearranging polities into new configurations.”</p>\r\n<p>I enjoyed Maxim Samson, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Earth-Shapers-Mapped-Mastered-Panama/dp/0226844749/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3376OGXZ1IW08&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.xY94trVzgBUqCcmTAs2eBw.PAoA1kI3tZTemS0qO2JBro1wpU4X9OQLjFOkOux4B2I&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Earth+Shapers%3A+How+We+Mapped+and+Mastered+the+World%2C+From+the+Panama+Canal+to+the+Baltic+Way&amp;qid=1759277918&amp;sprefix=earth+shapers+how+we+mapped+and+mastered+the+world%2C+from+the+panama+canal+to+the+baltic+way%2Caps%2C72&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Earth Shapers: How We Mapped and Mastered the World, From the Panama Canal to the Baltic Way</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/10/what-ive-been-reading-277.html\">What I’ve been reading</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/925707980/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/925707980/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a